{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790298892,"nonce":"7X3Hlu/NxE8uiWwmmeO1n0J4Lcc=","title":"Async poll functions store a value with no definition after the inliner change 717bf598","message":"Five tests in crates/zyntax_embed/tests/async_runtime_tests.rs fail on main (90840c39) and on perf-integration: test_execute_async_await_long_running_process, test_execute_async_chain_with_await, test_execute_async_function_with_promise, test_execute_async_with_await_in_loop, promise_combinator_tests::test_promise_all_with_nested_await. Each panics in the Cranelift backend (cranelift_backend.rs, HirInstruction::Store) with \"store in `\u003cfn\u003e$poll`: no value for its value HirId(N)\", for example `add_to_sum$poll`, `step2$poll`, `outer$poll`.\n\nReproducer (Mac, default features):\nRUST_MIN_STACK=134217728 cargo test -p zyntax_embed --test async_runtime_tests -- --test-threads=2\n\ngit bisect between 678f49eb (49/49 pass) and b503e8c1 (44/49) names 717bf598 \"Inliner: cold error paths and allocations do not make a callee call-bearing\" (git-bug 4e3f96c) as the first bad commit. Likely shape: a callee now inlines into an async function before the async state-machine lowering, and a value the inlined body defines is saved across an await into the poll fn's state without its definition reaching the poll fn.\n\nThis fails the CI \"native tests\" job (cargo test --workspace --lib --bins --tests) on every target once the build errors ahead of it are fixed.","files":null}]}